# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (April 2026), NVIDIA's NVFP4 build: 35B with 3B active,
# 23 GB, Apache-2.0. The sparse sibling of the dense 27B: the same hybrid
# layout, full attention in a quarter of the layers, with a mixture-of-experts
# feed-forward, so it should decode several times faster. It thinks by default
# (qwen3 reasoning parser) and calls tools (qwen3_xml parser). 256k natively;
# VLLM_LONG stretches it with the YaRN setting from Qwen's card.
# Flags are NVIDIA's DGX Spark recipe, except the cache, which stays at 16 bits.
TITLE="Qwen3.6-35B-A3B"
DETAIL="35B, 3B active, NVFP4, 23 GB"
HF_REPO=nvidia/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4
SERVED_NAME=qwen3.6-35b-a3b
MAX_LEN=262144
LONG_MAX_LEN=1010000
ROPE_ORIG=262144
ROPE_STYLE=qwen35
TOOL_PARSER=qwen3_xml
REASONING_PARSER=qwen3
# 10 of 40 layers are full attention with 2 KV heads of 256: about 21 KB per
# token at 16 bits, 20 GiB for the whole 1.01M window. 0.50 of 121.7 GiB gives
# the cache nearly twice that, so a prompt that fills the window has headroom.
KV_DTYPE=auto
MEM_UTIL=0.50
MIN_FREE_GB=62
EXTRA_ARGS="--trust-remote-code --attention-backend flashinfer --moe-backend marlin --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 --enable-chunked-prefill"
